margo 4.1.0 parses the `ignore_maximize` window rule but never reads it, and
maximize_request turns every set_maximized into fullscreen. Chromium-based
browsers restore a saved maximized state on every new window, so they open
fullscreen. Honour the rule for maximize and unmaximize requests, matched on
the toplevel's identity at request time (before the deferred initial map).

--- a/margo/src/state/handlers/xdg_shell.rs
+++ b/margo/src/state/handlers/xdg_shell.rs
@@ -547,6 +547,10 @@
     }
 
